# H1b (SOFT, card M only): the TIMED pass of H1 (watcher OFF). The same construction as H1a; five arms in interleaved rounds (30 timed rounds after 5 warm-ups, rotated and alternately reversed because the
# clock drifts): the target trace alone, the drafter trace alone, BOTH CONCURRENTLY (queue 0 and queue 1, non-blocking replays, then a per-sub-device synchronise of each queue), CHAINED by an event
# (target, record_event on queue 0, queue 1 waits, drafter), and BOTH ON ONE QUEUE (the control). The manager's create, load and clear times are recorded over several cycles. Outputs are compared byte for
# byte against the solo runs after every arm, after a stress of repeated concurrent replays and after the timed loop.
# PASS = concurrent wall <= 1.1 x max(solo walls), outputs identical, no hang: concurrent sub-device queues then cost a verify block max(V, D) instead of V + D, and the split is worth taking to the
# cores. FAIL-SERIALISED (the concurrent wall within 90 percent of t + d) = the queues did not overlap at all; FAIL-PARTIAL = some overlap (the DRAM and NoC contention or a shared dispatcher) but more than
# 1.1 x the longer solo: read 'overlap' in the JSON (1.0 = the shorter trace fully hidden) and 'one_queue_over_sum' (what a single queue already overlaps by itself).
# READ: the line 'SUBDEV_H1 verdict=...' with ratio, conc_ms, t_ms, d_ms, chained_ms, one_queue_ms, load_ms, clear_ms, split and grid; the last stdout line is the JSON (kind subdev-h1).
# TIMED: pause the ARC runners as for any timing arm (CI on the rig skews it). Duration (estimate): 25 min (the container timeout is 60 min).
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the sub-device overlap programme (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of
# the window branch (a branch that carries optimisation/ttnn-op/subdev_h and scripts/ci/tp4_subdev_probe.py) and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a
# registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch by its author. ORDER.txt has the order, the stop rules, the read rules and the minutes.
# C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next2-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag of the window's own image (sed -i 's/tp4-next2-1/<tag>/' *.env): this pack builds nothing, and any C2 image carries the tt-metal sub-device bindings
# it needs (the harnesses mount this checkout's files). The cards are under development: nothing here stops, starts or hands back the node agent.

C2_CARDS=pair
C2_ACTIONS=cardm
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next2-1
C2_CARDM_HARNESS=optimisation/ttnn-op/subdev_h/run_card_m.sh
C2_CARDM_ENV=IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next2-1
